From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sailfish: force simulated DSI panel for headless boot

The Pixel bootloader always appends the real sailfish panel name to the
kernel command line, so a boot-image override is ignored. Force the
matching panel into SIM_SW_TE_MODE after DT lookup so panel reads, ACK
waits, ESD checks, and hardware TE waits do not block without a display.

This still registers a valid MDSS display 0 for SurfaceFlinger/HWC.
---
 drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_dsi.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_dsi.c b/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_dsi.c
--- a/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_dsi.c
@@ -2791,5 +2791,12 @@ static struct device_node *mdss_dsi_find_panel_of_node(
 			goto end;
 		} else {
+			if (!strcmp(panel_name,
+				"qcom,mdss_dsi_samsung_ea8064tg_1080p_cmd")) {
+				pinfo->sim_panel_mode = SIM_SW_TE_MODE;
+				pr_info("%s: forcing sailfish SIM_SW_TE_MODE\n",
+					__func__);
+			}
+
 			/* extract config node name if present */
 			str1 += i;
 			str2 = strnstr(str1, "config", strlen(str1));
